#!/usr/bin/python3
"""nu-vpn: hands-off GlobalProtect (SAML) sign-in for NetworkManager.

When you click Connect on the VPN in Plasma's network applet, NetworkManager
asks its secret agents for the VPN cookie. `nu-vpn agent` is registered after
Plasma's agent, so NetworkManager asks it first. It then:

  1. asks the GlobalProtect portal where to sign in (Microsoft Entra SAML),
  2. drives a hidden WebKit view: fills in the username and the password from
     your keyring, accepts "Stay signed in?" and Duo's "Is this your device?",
  3. pops up one small box for the Duo Mobile passcode, if Duo asks for one
     (no box at all when the remembered Microsoft/Duo session still holds),
  4. has openconnect turn the SAML result into a gateway cookie, and
  5. hands cookie/gateway/certificate back to NetworkManager, which connects.

If a page shows up that it doesn't know how to handle, the hidden browser
window is shown so you can finish by hand. Cancelling the code box cancels
the connection. Any other failure falls back to Plasma's usual dialog.

Subcommands:
  setup    save your username (config file) and password (keyring)
  login    run the sign-in once and print what happened (for debugging)
  agent    run the NetworkManager secret agent (the systemd user service)
  connect  bring the VPN up through NetworkManager (same as clicking Connect)
  forget   clear the remembered Microsoft/Duo browser session
"""

